<!-- quality_gate agent contract — start -->
## Quality Gate agent contract

Run `bundle exec quality_gate fast` after Ruby edits. Run `bundle exec quality_gate verify` before you finish a change, and `bundle exec quality_gate audit` before you merge security-sensitive work.

Fix findings before you continue editing.

- Exit 0 means the gate ran clean.
- Exit 1 means the gate reported findings and no tool failures.
- Exit 2 means the gate could not complete cleanly because of invalid input, configuration, or another tool failure.

The default fast path keeps feedback tight with a 10-second RuboCop timeout. Verify and audit keep the broader suite work on the 120-second default timeout.

<% if agent_option?(:agents) %>Installed Claude Code hooks can run `bundle exec quality_gate verify` automatically at session end. If those hooks become unavailable, inspect `log/quality_gate_hooks.jsonl`, run `bundle install`, and reinstall them with `bin/rails generate quality_gate:install --agents`.
<% end %><% if agent_option?(:codex) %>
The optional Codex Stop hook runs the full `verify` gate on every Stop, which can add noticeable latency. Findings request one repair continuation; Codex reruns verification on the resumed Stop, and remaining findings are reported while allowing the turn to finish. Hook failures are reported as unavailable and also allow the turn to finish. Keep the direct manual gate and CI checks as enforcement evidence.

Enable this project hook only in a trusted project. In Codex, review the hook through `/hooks`, inspect `.codex/hooks/quality_gate_verify_stop.rb` and the generated command in `.codex/hooks.json`, then explicitly trust it. Quality Gate never changes Codex trust settings. Doctor cannot confirm hook trust, activation, or execution history.

To refresh the generated Codex hook after a Quality Gate upgrade that changes its launcher or hook configuration, run `bin/rails generate quality_gate:install --codex`.

If the project moves, update the absolute command in `.codex/hooks.json` and review trust again. Resolve a custom `hooks.json` manually using the proposed configuration printed by the installer. To remove the integration, remove Quality Gate's Stop entry and script; remove `.codex/hooks.json` only when it contains solely generated Quality Gate configuration. Remove only the Codex-specific instructions from `AGENTS.md` when it also contains Claude guidance, or remove the Quality Gate section when Codex is its only client.
<% else %>
Other clients, including Codex, must run `bundle exec quality_gate verify` manually before you finish a change.
<% end %>
<!-- quality_gate agent contract — end -->
